# L §7.6 item 2 (tally 2.1.6, issue #89): a range an aggregate steps through holds at most 1 000 000 keys; with
# literal ends, which load sees (§2.5), 1..1000001 is LOAD-LIMIT, which stops the reality. tally 2.1.5's refcore
# answered 500 001 500 001. (The edge, 1..1000000, costs seconds here; T's vectors hold it.)
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
ask r: sum(k for k in 1..1000001)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LIMIT 1 .. 1 000 001 holds more than 1 000 000 keys (m.tally:9)
